{"id":443505971,"author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOR1LuPM4ab10z","tag_name":"v0.52.667","target_commitish":"master","name":"v0.52.667","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-11-12T21:02:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T21:06:41Z","published_at":"2026-11-12T21:02:54Z","assets":[],"body":"## Known issues\n- **Context meter after a reload or model switch (#8975).** For some sessions on custom or self-hosted endpoints, the\n  context meter can show the default window (256K) instead of the model's real window after a page reload or a model\n  switch. It corrects itself on the next turn. Compression and chats are unaffected. Context-management plugins that\n  read WebUI's context window see the same default until then.\n- Credentials can pair with the wrong URL on Agent builds after hermes-agent #151775 when a providers: entry named like a built-in provider has its own URL and model.base_url differs (#8973, Form 3). Present in every release; fix in progress.\n\n\n## What's Changed\n* release: #8903 `TestConflictError` no longer fails in focused or partial test runs (#8903) by @nesquena-hermes in https://github.com/nesquena/hermes-webui/pull/8998\n* test: TestConflictError starts with no registered chat runs (order-dependent failure in focused runs) by @nesquena-hermes in https://github.com/nesquena/hermes-webui/pull/8903\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/nesquena/hermes-webui/compare/exp-v0.52.666...v0.52.667\n","mentions_count":1}
